	(text "Supervised arm:\nArming needs agreement of both MCUs. ARM_GATE is driven from VBAT_CON by Q13;\nQ13's base is pulled down only through Q14 and Q12 in series: Q14 from the OC's\nOC_ARM_EN, Q12 from the FC's FC_ARM via R132. Both must be driven high. An MCU\nthat is off, in reset, or high-Z holds its transistor off through the built-in\n47k base-emitter resistor, and R22 bleeds the gate in ~0.2 ms. GPIO44 has a weak\npull-up at reset, so the OC term is the fail-safe: OC firmware raises OC_ARM_EN\nonly during a fire test or real flight. R139 limits Q13's collector current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130.175 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "135fe8c4-3e26-4e87-ae16-04055c2896c4")
	)
